opes, each read against its own record rather than a document-wide table: a component's own `power_units` (against that component's `base_power`), a cost payload's own `power_units` (e.g. `CostCurve`, against the owning component's `base_power`), and a time series association's own `unit_system` (governing only that one series).\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"UpDown\":{\"description\":\"A pair of values, one for the upward (`up`) and one for the downward (`down`) direction of a quantity.\",\"properties\":{\"down\":{\"title\":\"Down\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"up\":{\"title\":\"Up\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"up\",\"down\"],\"title\":\"UpDown\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"ValueCurve\":{\"description\":\"A cost or fuel curve: function data plus a declaration of how to read its y axis. `INPUT_OUTPUT` reads y as the total `f(x)`, `INCREMENTAL` as the marginal rate `f'(x)`, and `AVERAGE_RATE` as the average `f(x)/x`; the three can express the same underlying function and are inter-convertible given `initial_input`. The `TIME_SERIES_*` variants are the time-varying equivalents. Which form to use follows the data source: bid stacks are incremental, total cost tables input-output, efficiency tables average rate.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"AVERAGE_RATE\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/AverageRateCurve\",\"INCREMENTAL\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/IncrementalCurve\",\"INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/InputOutputCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_AVERAGE_RATE\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\"},\"propertyName\":\"curve_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/InputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/IncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/AverageRateCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-b2dfc14680f34633e5b1.json#/\$defs/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\"}],\"title\":\"ValueCurve\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"XY_Coords\":{\"description\":\"A single point, given as its `x` and `y` coordinates.\",\"properties\":{\"x\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"x-curve-dimension\":[0,1],\"description\":\"Units: the wrapped function's input unit.\"},\"y\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"x-curve-dimension\":[1,0],\"description\":\"Units: the wrapped function's output unit.\"}},\"required\":[\"x\",\"y\"],\"title\":\"XY_Coords\",\"type\":\"object\"}}}",
